---
import FutureTechMissionFrame from '../../../../components/FutureTechMissionFrame.astro';
---
<FutureTechMissionFrame
  missionNumber="3"
  title="Build a Game"
  tagline="Turn code into a game another person can play."
  question="How can I combine controls, rules, score and testing to make a game another person can play?"
  success="I can create a playable timing game, use a controller input to trigger a rule, change score or end the game, and improve the game after a playtest."
>
  <div class="game-flow" aria-label="Mission game flow"><span>MOVE</span><b>→</b><span>PRESS</span><b>→</b><span>CHECK</span><b>→</b><span>SCORE / END</span></div>
  <p class="flow-note">Both controller paths use the same game idea. The hardware and blocks may look different.</p>

  <section id="stage-1" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">01</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">GET READY</p><h2 class="stage-title">Set Up</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Grab your usual micro:bit kit and find your assigned controller station. You will work through this mission independently and stay on the same controller path for the whole mission.</p>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ Computer</span><span>☐ micro:bit V2</span><span>☐ USB data cable</span><span>☐ Assigned controller</span><span>☐ Mission page open</span></div>
    <p class="success"><b>Individual mission:</b> you are responsible for building, testing, and explaining your own game. You will work with another student only when a peer check or playtest is useful.</p>

    <p class="mini-label">Your controller path</p>
    <div class="path-grid">
      <article class="path-card path-a"><div class="path-top"><span class="path-badge">PATH A</span><span class="device-label">5×5 LED / :GAME</span></div><h3>Kitronik :GAME Controller</h3><dl><div><dt>Editor</dt><dd>micro:bit MakeCode</dd></div><div><dt>Action button</dt><dd>Fire 1</dd></div><div><dt>Display</dt><dd>micro:bit 5×5 LEDs</dd></div></dl><strong class="stay-label">STAY ON PATH A</strong></article>
      <article class="path-card path-b"><div class="path-top"><span class="path-badge">PATH B</span><span class="device-label">SCREEN / RETRO</span></div><h3>ELECFREAKS Retro Arcade</h3><dl><div><dt>Editor</dt><dd>MakeCode Arcade</dd></div><div><dt>Action button</dt><dd>A</dd></div><div><dt>Display</dt><dd>Colour screen</dd></div></dl><strong class="stay-label">STAY ON PATH B</strong></article>
    </div>
    <p class="concept">Your teacher will assign a station such as <b>A1</b>, <b>A2</b>, <b>B1</b>, or <b>B2</b>. If controllers need to be shared, use your assigned station when it is available, but keep your own project and code. Do not switch controller type during this mission. Your checkpoint is based on the game ideas, not which controller you used.</p>
    <div class="my-path" aria-label="Path memory aid"><strong>MY PATH</strong><span><b>A</b> · :GAME · micro:bit MakeCode · Fire 1</span><span><b>B</b> · RETRO · MakeCode Arcade · A button</span></div>

    <p class="mini-label">Quick Reboot</p>
    <div class="reboot"><span>EVENT</span><span>IF</span><span>LOOP</span></div>
    <p class="success">✓ You are ready when you know your Path A/B assignment and the game rule: <b>move → press → decide → score/end</b>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-2" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">02</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">FIRST GAME MOTION</p><h2 class="stage-title">First Code</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">First, make something move. Do not add score, target logic, or controller actions yet.</p>
    <div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>1 — Create</strong><p>Start <code>FirstName_L1_M3</code> and create one visible game object.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>2 — Move</strong><p>Make the object move horizontally and keep moving repeatedly.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>3 — Keep it playable</strong><p>Keep it in the visible game area and slow it enough for a player to react.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>4 — Simulate</strong><p>Test the moving object before you add scoring or controller rules.</p></article></div>
    <div class="path-reminder"><strong>READ ONLY YOUR PATH</strong><span>A = :GAME / micro:bit MakeCode</span><span>B = Retro Arcade / MakeCode Arcade</span></div>

    <div class="path-grid path-work">
      <article class="path-card path-a">
        <div class="path-top"><span class="path-badge">PATH A</span><span class="device-label">5×5 LED / :GAME</span></div><h3>LED Target Snap</h3><p><b>YOUR NEXT STEP:</b> Open <a class="external" href="https://makecode.microbit.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">micro:bit MakeCode ↗</a> and create <code>FirstName_L1_M3</code>.</p>
        <div class="block-finder"><span><b>Game</b> → create sprite</span><span><b>Loops</b> → forever</span><span><b>Game</b> → move</span><span><b>Game</b> → if on edge, bounce</span><span><b>Basic</b> → pause</span></div>
        <aside class="code-model" aria-label="Path A movement code model"><div class="code-model-head"><span>CODE MODEL 1 OF 4</span><strong>Make one LED dot move</strong></div><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block event">on start</div><div class="mk-block variables indent">set <span class="value">player</span> to create sprite at <span class="value">x 0, y 2</span></div><div class="mk-gap"></div><div class="mk-block loops">forever</div><div class="mk-block game indent">player move <span class="value">1</span></div><div class="mk-block game indent">player if on edge, bounce</div><div class="mk-block basic indent">pause <span class="value">300 ms</span></div></div><p class="code-model-note">The starting side and speed can change. The important idea is that <b>move + bounce + pause stay inside forever</b>.</p></aside>
        <p class="success">✓ One LED dot moves back and forth without you pressing a button.</p><p class="warning">Dot only moves once? Check <b>forever</b>. Too fast? Increase the <b>pause</b>.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="path-card path-b">
        <div class="path-top"><span class="path-badge">PATH B</span><span class="device-label">SCREEN / RETRO</span></div><h3>Arcade Target Snap</h3><p><b>YOUR NEXT STEP:</b> Open <a class="external" href="https://arcade.makecode.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MakeCode Arcade ↗</a> and create <code>FirstName_L1_M3</code>.</p>
        <div class="block-finder"><span><b>Sprites</b> → set mySprite to sprite of kind Player</span><span><b>Sprites</b> → set velocity vx / vy</span><span><b>Sprites</b> → set bounce on wall ON</span></div>
        <aside class="code-model" aria-label="Path B movement code model"><div class="code-model-head"><span>CODE MODEL 2 OF 4</span><strong>Make one simple sprite move</strong></div><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block arcade">on start</div><div class="mk-block sprites indent">set <span class="value">player</span> to sprite of kind <span class="value">Player</span></div><div class="mk-block sprites indent">set player velocity to <span class="value">vx 40, vy 0</span></div><div class="mk-block sprites indent">set player bounce on wall <span class="value">ON</span></div></div><p class="code-model-note">Keep the sprite image simple. Mission 3 is about the game rule, not artwork.</p></aside>
        <p class="success">✓ One sprite moves left and right across the screen without you pressing A.</p><p class="warning">Sprite disappears? Check <b>bounce on wall</b>. Too fast? Lower the horizontal velocity.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="success full-success"><b>Both paths are ready for Stage 3</b> when a game object moves repeatedly without the player pressing the action button.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-3" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">03</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">INPUT → RULE → RESULT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Make It React</h2></div></div>
    <div class="route"><span>PRESS</span><span>CHECK TARGET</span><span>TRUE: SCORE</span><span>FALSE: END</span></div>
    <div class="path-reminder"><strong>STAY ON YOUR PATH</strong><span>A = :GAME / Fire 1</span><span>B = Retro Arcade / A button</span></div>

    <div class="path-grid path-work">
      <article class="path-card path-a">
        <div class="path-top"><span class="path-badge">PATH A</span><span class="device-label">5×5 LED / :GAME</span></div><h3>PATH A STUDENTS — CONTINUE HERE</h3>
        <p><b>First, familiar input:</b> make the target rule work with micro:bit <b>Button A</b>.</p>
        <div class="block-finder"><span><b>Input</b> → on button A pressed</span><span><b>Game</b> → get x</span><span><b>Logic</b> → if / =</span><span><b>Game</b> → add score</span><span><b>Game</b> → game over</span></div>
        <aside class="code-model" aria-label="Path A scoring rule code model"><div class="code-model-head"><span>CODE MODEL 3 OF 4</span><strong>Button A checks the centre</strong></div><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block input">on button <span class="value">A</span> pressed</div><div class="mk-block logic indent">if <span class="value">player x = 2</span> then</div><div class="mk-block game indent2">add score <span class="value">1</span></div><div class="mk-block logic indent">else</div><div class="mk-block game indent2">game over</div></div><p class="code-model-note"><b>x = 2</b> means the centre LED column. Later you can change the target.</p></aside>
        <div class="predict-grid"><span><b>If player x = 2</b><small>Predict: what happens?</small></span><span><b>If player x ≠ 2</b><small>Predict: what happens?</small></span></div>
        <p class="success">✓ Button A scores at the centre and ends the round when the dot is not at the centre.</p>

        <div class="hardware-card"><strong>CONNECT YOUR :GAME CONTROLLER</strong><ol><li><b>Power off first.</b> Insert the micro:bit firmly into the edge connector. Do not force it.</li><li><b>Action button:</b> Fire 1.</li><li><b>MakeCode:</b> add the <b>Kitronik :GAME Controller</b> extension. Use <b>on button Fire 1 (P15) press down</b>.</li><li><b>Test first:</b> if needed, temporarily make Fire 1 show an icon.</li></ol><p><b>Replace the input event. Keep the IF rule the same.</b></p></div>
        <p class="success">✓ Fire 1 now triggers the same score/end rule that Button A triggered.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="path-card path-b">
        <div class="path-top"><span class="path-badge">PATH B</span><span class="device-label">SCREEN / RETRO</span></div><h3>PATH B STUDENTS — CONTINUE HERE</h3>
        <div class="hardware-card"><strong>RETRO ARCADE SETUP</strong><ol><li>Insert the micro:bit V2 securely. Do not force it.</li><li>Open <b>Microsoft MakeCode Arcade</b>.</li><li>Use the prepared micro:bit V2 / Retro Arcade hardware target.</li><li><b>Action button:</b> A.</li></ol><p>If A works in the simulator but not on the physical unit, check the hardware target, newest download, and micro:bit seating.</p></div>
        <p><b>Your target zone is the right side of the screen.</b> Press A when the moving sprite reaches that side.</p>
        <div class="block-finder"><span><b>Controller</b> → on A button pressed</span><span><b>Sprites</b> → mySprite x</span><span><b>Logic</b> → if / &gt;</span><span><b>Info</b> → change score by</span><span><b>Game</b> → game over</span></div>
        <aside class="code-model" aria-label="Path B scoring rule code model"><div class="code-model-head"><span>CODE MODEL 4 OF 4</span><strong>A checks the right-side target</strong></div><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block controller">on <span class="value">A</span> button pressed</div><div class="mk-block logic indent">if <span class="value">player x &gt; 120</span> then</div><div class="mk-block info indent2">change score by <span class="value">1</span></div><div class="mk-block logic indent">else</div><div class="mk-block arcade indent2">game over</div></div><p class="code-model-note">The sprite's <b>x</b> value is its horizontal position. <b>x &gt; 120</b> makes the far-right side of the screen the beginner target zone.</p></aside>
        <div class="predict-grid"><span><b>If player x &gt; 120</b><small>Predict: what happens?</small></span><span><b>If player x ≤ 120</b><small>Predict: what happens?</small></span></div>
        <p class="success">✓ Pressing A on the right side scores. Pressing A too early ends the round.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="concept">The button does not decide whether you win. <b>The IF rule decides.</b> The button only triggers the check.</p>
    <p class="success full-success">✓ Your assigned controller can now trigger a working score/end decision.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-4" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">04</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">YOUR GAME</p><h2 class="stage-title">Build It — Timing Target Game</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Turn the guided example into a game another student can play. Keep the core game simple, then make at least one meaningful choice of your own.</p>
    <div class="gcr-grid"><article><strong>GOAL</strong><p>Press at the right moment to score.</p></article><article><strong>CONTROL</strong><p>Fire 1 or A — use your assigned path.</p></article><article><strong>RULE</strong><p>IF the moving object is at/in the target → score. Otherwise → end.</p></article></div>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ One visible moving game object</span><span>☐ Movement repeats continuously</span><span>☐ One physical controller action</span><span>☐ One clear target/success rule</span><span>☐ One IF decision</span><span>☐ Success increases score</span><span>☐ Failure ends the round/game</span><span>☐ Game works on physical hardware</span><span>☐ Player can understand the game quickly</span><span>☐ At least one meaningful personalization</span><span>☐ Another student playtested it</span><span>☐ We improved one thing and retested</span></div>
    <p class="mini-label">Make one meaningful choice</p>
    <div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>Speed</strong><p>Make the timing easier or harder.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Target</strong><p>Change where or when success happens.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Score</strong><p>Change how many points success earns.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Theme</strong><p>Change the look or message without changing the core rule.</p></article></div>
    <p class="success">✓ <b>Build It is ready when:</b> another student can understand the goal, use the controller, experience success and failure, and you can explain one improvement you made after testing.</p>

    <p class="mini-label">Playtest and improve</p>
    <div class="playtest-flow"><span><b>PLAY</b><small>Player tries once without creator help.</small></span><i>→</i><span><b>NOTICE</b><small>Was the goal clear? Was timing fair? Did score/failure work?</small></span><i>→</i><span><b>CHANGE</b><small>Improve one thing based on what happened.</small></span><i>→</i><span><b>RETEST</b><small>Try again and see if the change helped.</small></span></div>

    <div class="try4"><strong>STUCK? TRY 4</strong><p>1. CHECK — blocks, values, order, and nesting. 2. SIMULATE the newest version. 3. DOWNLOAD the newest version. 4. PARTNER — briefly explain expected vs actual to a nearby student. Still stuck? Ask for help and say what you already tried.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-5" class="stage">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">05</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">OPTIONAL CHALLENGE</p><h2 class="stage-title">Level It Up</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Only after every Build It requirement works. Choose <b>one</b> while you wait for your checkpoint.</p>
    <div class="level-grid"><article class="level-card"><strong>Speed Tuner</strong><p>Change movement speed and decide which version is most playable.</p></article><article class="level-card"><strong>Random Target</strong><p>Use randomness to change the target position/location between rounds.</p></article><article class="level-card"><strong>Two Controls</strong><p>Add one second meaningful controller action.</p></article><article class="level-card"><strong>Win Goal</strong><p>Add a simple score target or another clear ending rule.</p></article></div>
    <p class="warning"><b>Mission 3 limit:</b> do not add advanced Arcade scenes, enemies, tilemaps, or multiple levels yet.</p>
    <p class="success">When every Build It box is checked and your improvement is retested, add your name to the <b>Ready-for-Check</b> queue. Keep Leveling Up until you are called.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="stage-6" class="stage checkpoint">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">06</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SHOW WHAT YOU KNOW</p><h2 class="stage-title">Checkpoint</h2></div></div>
    <p class="intro">Bring your controller and open your code when you are called. The checkpoint is individual: you demonstrate, explain, change, and test your own game.</p>
    <div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>Check 1 — Play / Identify</strong><p>Demonstrate the game. Point to the physical action button and the code event that responds to it.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Check 2 — Explain the System</strong><p>Explain what keeps the object moving, what the IF rule checks, what success does to the score, and what causes the game to end.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Check 3 — Change It</strong><p>Change target position/location, movement speed, scoring amount/behaviour, or the action button. Predict first, then test.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>After Your Check</strong><p><b>MISSION COMPLETE</b> · <b>RETRY ONE SKILL</b> · <b>SUPPORT ROUTE</b></p></article></div>
  </section>

  <section class="stage passport">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">✓</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SKILL PASSPORT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Mission 3 Skills</h2></div></div>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ I can create and move a game object.</span><span>☐ I can use repeated code to keep a game active.</span><span>☐ I can use a controller button to trigger a game action.</span><span>☐ I can use an IF rule to change score or end a game.</span><span>☐ I can playtest a game and make one useful improvement.</span><span>☐ I can change, test, and explain my game independently.</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="stage reset">
    <div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">↺</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">LEAVE IT READY</p><h2 class="stage-title">Reset</h2></div></div>
    <div class="check-list"><span>☐ Project saved correctly</span><span>☐ micro:bit returned to numbered kit</span><span>☐ USB cable returned and loosely coiled</span><span>☐ Controller returned to its labelled station</span><span>☐ Workspace clear</span><span>☐ Faults or damage reported</span><span>☐ Passport/progress updated</span></div>
    <p class="concept">Exit question: What made your game fair—or unfair—to the player?</p>
  </section>
</FutureTechMissionFrame>

<style is:global>
.game-flow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:.55rem;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:.7rem .8rem;border-radius:12px;background:#111827;color:#fff;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.04em}.game-flow span{padding:.35rem .55rem;border-radius:999px;background:#312e81;color:#e0e7ff}.game-flow b{color:#67e8f9}.flow-note{margin:.45rem 0 1rem;text-align:center;color:#667085;font-size:.84rem;font-weight:700}
.path-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.7rem;margin:.7rem 0}.path-card{min-width:0;padding:.9rem;border:2px solid #dbe3ef;border-radius:16px;background:#fff}.path-card.path-a{border-color:#c4b5fd;background:linear-gradient(145deg,#fff,#faf8ff)}.path-card.path-b{border-color:#a5f3fc;background:linear-gradient(145deg,#fff,#f0fdff)}.path-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}.path-badge,.device-label{display:inline-flex;padding:.28rem .5rem;border-radius:999px;font-size:.67rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.06em}.path-a .path-badge{background:#5b21b6;color:#fff}.path-b .path-badge{background:#0e7490;color:#fff}.device-label{background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569}.path-card h3{margin:.65rem 0 .4rem;color:#172033;font-size:1.08rem}.path-card p{color:#59677c;line-height:1.48;font-size:.9rem}.path-card dl{margin:.45rem 0;display:grid;gap:.28rem}.path-card dl div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:100px 1fr;gap:.5rem}.path-card dt{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:900;color:#64748b;text-transform:uppercase}.path-card dd{margin:0;color:#25324a;font-weight:750}.stay-label{display:inline-block;margin-top:.45rem;color:#5b21b6;font-size:.76rem;letter-spacing:.05em}.path-b .stay-label{color:#0e7490}
.my-path,.path-reminder{display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.7rem 0;padding:.6rem .7rem;border:1px solid #dbe3ef;border-radius:11px;background:#f8fafc;color:#475569;font-size:.8rem}.my-path>strong,.path-reminder>strong{color:#172033}.my-path span,.path-reminder span{padding:.28rem .45rem;border-radius:999px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0}.reboot{display:flex;gap:.45rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.3rem 0 .6rem}.reboot span{padding:.4rem .65rem;border-radius:999px;background:#ede9fe;color:#5b21b6;font-weight:900;font-size:.76rem}
.block-finder{display:flex;gap:.38rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.65rem 0}.block-finder span{padding:.34rem .5rem;border:1px solid #dbe3ef;border-radius:999px;background:#fff;color:#52617a;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:750}.block-finder b{color:#5b21b6}.path-b .block-finder b{color:#0e7490}
.code-model{margin:.7rem 0;padding:.8rem;border:1px solid #c7d2fe;border-radius:14px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f8faff,#f5f3ff)}.path-b .code-model{border-color:#a5f3fc;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f8fdff,#ecfeff)}.code-model-head{display:grid;gap:.15rem;margin-bottom:.55rem}.code-model-head span{color:#6d28d9;font:900 .64rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.08em}.path-b .code-model-head span{color:#0e7490}.code-model-head strong{color:#26324a;font-size:.86rem}.code-stack{display:grid;gap:.27rem;padding:.6rem;border-radius:11px;background:#111827;overflow:hidden}.mk-block{width:max-content;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:.46rem .58rem;border-radius:7px;color:#fff;font:800 .72rem/1.25 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.mk-block.event{background:#7c3aed}.mk-block.variables{background:#dc2626}.mk-block.loops{background:#15803d}.mk-block.game{background:#0891b2}.mk-block.basic{background:#2563eb}.mk-block.input{background:#c026d3}.mk-block.logic{background:#059669}.mk-block.arcade{background:#7c3aed}.mk-block.sprites{background:#0e7490}.mk-block.controller{background:#c026d3}.mk-block.info{background:#2563eb}.mk-block.indent{margin-left:.75rem}.mk-block.indent2{margin-left:1.5rem}.mk-block .value{display:inline-block;margin-left:.14rem;padding:.04rem .25rem;border-radius:4px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.2)}.mk-gap{height:.12rem}.code-model-note{margin:.55rem 0 0!important;color:#59677c!important;font-size:.8rem!important;line-height:1.42!important}.hardware-card{margin:.7rem 0;padding:.75rem;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #dbe3ef;background:#fff}.hardware-card>strong{display:block;color:#172033;font-size:.78rem;letter-spacing:.04em}.hardware-card ol{margin:.45rem 0 .3rem;padding-left:1.2rem;color:#52617a;font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.45}.hardware-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0!important;font-size:.82rem!important}
.predict-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.4rem;margin:.55rem 0}.predict-grid span{padding:.55rem;border-radius:9px;background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0}.predict-grid b{display:block;color:#172033;font-size:.78rem}.predict-grid small{color:#64748b}.full-success{margin-top:.85rem!important}
